#37113
Intersection of Black Mountain Road and Sapphire Street~
   The security here is almost non-existent with a few elemental archers placed
every so often.  Even they seem to take the job a little less seriously.  A
large gate is embedded into the wall to the south and serves no purpose other
than to give the room the feeling of being able to go south.  The road continues
east and west.  A road leading north allows for a clear view of the center of
the city.  The mountains to the north give this area a stunning view.
~
