#37154
Sapphire Street~
   The southern wall is made only out of stone, unlike the onyx that makes up
the northern.  Large holes in the wall serve as windows and lookouts into the
great body of water to the south.  The security here is almost non-existent with
a few elemental archers placed every so often.  Even they seem to take the job a
little less seriously.  The road continues east and west.
~
